{"title":"List of United States elementary school mathematics competitions","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"National_elementary_school_mathematics_competitions\">National elementary school mathematics competitions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=List_of_United_States_elementary_school_mathematics_competitions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: National elementary school mathematics competitions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://competifyhub.com/compete/\">Junior Championship</a> is one of the largest international elementary school math competition in the world.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://Perennialmath.com\">Perennial Math</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Continental_Mathematics_League\" title=\"Continental Mathematics League\">Continental Mathematics League</a> (CML)</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.mindresearch.org/gameathon/\">Game-a-thon</a> challenges students to design and build math games in this national contest.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Noetic_Learning_Math_Contest\" title=\"Noetic Learning Math Contest\">Noetic Learning Math Contest</a> - semiannual problem solving contest for elementary and middle school students. [Grades 2-8]</li>\n<li>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_Bee\" title=\"Math Bee\">Math Bee</a> hosted by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=North_South_Foundation\" title=\"North South Foundation\">North South Foundation</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_Olympiads_for_Elementary_and_Middle_Schools\" title=\"Math Olympiads for Elementary and Middle Schools\">Math Olympiads for Elementary and Middle Schools</a> (MOEMS) -- An extremely popular competition amongst elementary and middle school students.  <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Z_lj8xIFRfw?si=oCLTDKn-q514-KGm\">Video</a>  <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.moems.org/\">Website</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_Kangaroo\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Math Kangaroo\">Math Kangaroo</a> may be the world's largest <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition\" title=\"Mathematics competition\">mathematics competition</a>.  <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Z_lj8xIFRfw?si=oCLTDKn-q514-KGm\">Video</a>  <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.mathkangaroo.org/mk/default.html\">Website</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Math_League\" title=\"Math League\">Math League</a> has different names in different states and regions.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.mathcon.org\">MathCON</a> hosts annual math competition for students in grades 4-12.</li>\n<li>Math Madness (<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.aretelabs.com/math_madness/about\">website</a>) (<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c122241\">AoPS Forum</a>) 100% Online league and bracket tournament held in the fall (Mini-Madness held in spring)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Beestar\" title=\"Beestar\">Beestar</a> Register NOW: challenges 1st to 8th grade students in data analysis and problem solving skills through <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.beestar.org/exercise/samples.jsp?adid=105\">Weekly Problem Solving Contests</a> and <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.beestar.org/competition/?adid=105\">Beestar National Competition(BNC)</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Online_Math_League\" title=\"Online Math League\">Online Math League</a> (OML)</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.mathnasium.com/trimathlon\">National Trimathlon</a> is a fun filled Math Competition for kids in grades 3 through 6.</li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://pimathcontest.com/\">Pi Math Contest</a> is a math competition for elementary, middle, and high school students.</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=RSM_Foundation_International_Math_Contest&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"RSM Foundation International Math Contest (page does not exist)\">RSM Foundation International Math Contest</a> is a two-round Olympiad-style contest for students in grades 1-8. (<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://contest.rsmfoundation.org/oly/registration\">website</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Online_Youth_Mathematics_Competition\" title=\"Online Youth Mathematics Competition\">Online Youth Mathematics Competition</a> (OYMC) is a three round contest for students 8th grade and under. There are two divisions: Elementary and Middle School Division. More information can be found in their website. (<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://oymcofficial.org/\">website link</a>)</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"State_elementary_school_mathematics_competitions\">State elementary school mathematics competitions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=List_of_United_States_elementary_school_mathematics_competitions&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: State elementary school mathematics competitions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Alabama_mathematics_competitions\" title=\"Alabama mathematics competitions\">Alabama mathematics competitions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Alaska_mathematics_competitions\" title=\"Alaska mathematics competitions\">Alaska mathematics competitions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Arizona_mathematics_competitions\" title=\"Arizona mathematics competitions\">Arizona mathematics competitions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Arkansas_mathematics_competitions\" title=\"Arkansas mathematics competitions\">Arkansas mathematics competitions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=California_mathematics_competitions\" title=\"California mathematics competitions\">California mathematics competitions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Colorado_mathematics_competitions\" title=\"Colorado mathematics competitions\">Colorado mathematics competitions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Connecticut_mathematics_competitions\" title=\"Connecticut mathematics competitions\">Connecticut mathematics competitions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Delaware_mathematics_competitions\" title=\"Delaware mathematics competitions\">Delaware mathematics competitions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Florida_mathematics_competitions\" title=\"Florida mathematics competitions\">Florida mathematics competitions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Georgia_mathematics_competitions\" title=\"Georgia mathematics competitions\">Georgia mathematics competitions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hawaii_mathematics_competitions\" title=\"Hawaii mathematics competitions\">Hawaii mathematics competitions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Idaho_mathematics_competitions\" title=\"Idaho mathematics competitions\">Idaho mathematics competitions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Illinois_mathematics_competitions\" title=\"Illinois mathematics competitions\">Illinois mathematics competitions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Indiana_mathematics_competitions\" title=\"Indiana mathematics competitions\">Indiana mathematics competitions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/